<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarentum</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Taras</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarentum, Greek Taras, was a Spartan colony founded around 706 BCE on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-taranto">Gulf of Taranto</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on the site of modern Taranto. With a fine harbour and rich trade, it became the leading Greek city of the region, heading the Italiote League from the fourth century BCE. Its call for help from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrrhus-of-epirus">Pyrrhus of Epirus</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> failed, and it fell to Rome in 272 BCE.</p></div>
